**id.cpp formats gamepad device identifiers and enum values for diagnostics.**

## Interface

- `operator<<(ostream&, device_id) -> ostream&`: emits `device(none)` for null, otherwise `device(<value>)`.
- `to_string(transport_kind) noexcept -> const char*`: maps `unknown`, `xinput`, `raw_input`, `hid` to `"unknown"`, `"xinput"`, `"raw-input"`, `"hid"`.
- `operator<<(ostream&, transport_kind) -> ostream&`: delegates to `to_string`.
- `to_string(connection) noexcept -> const char*`: maps `unknown`, `usb`, `bluetooth`, `virtualized` to matching strings.
- `operator<<(ostream&, connection) -> ostream&`: delegates to `to_string`.

## Coupling

`id.hpp` declares symbols in `gamepad::unstable::controller`; `ostream` formatting supports diagnostics. Unknown enum values fall back to `"unknown"`.